- /duplicates and /transfers each have their own page-level `<header>` (pre-existing,
  inside <main>, so per the HTML/ARIA spec they do NOT get the implicit "banner"
  role since they're descendants of <main> — only base.html's new header, which
  sits outside <main>, is the page's landmark banner). Axe found 0 violations on
  both pages — specifically no landmark/banner-duplication flag — confirming the
  new sitewide <header> wrap does not create a duplicate-banner regression.

